Hi Yuchao,

I was attempting to use Canopy (updated from github) to analyze a data set, and while sampling and BIC completed successfully, canopy.post <http://canopy.post> returned the following error message:
Error in 1:nrow(config.summary) : argument of length 0

Varying the burnin, thin, and post.config.cutoff doesn't appear to resolve the error. Do you have any advice as to what it might be?

Best wishes,
William

