Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi William,

The error that you saw was due to the fact that your MCMC has not converged yet. See the attached likelihood from 20 chains (4 were stuck in local mode). You need to let the chain run longer to get it converged. With the current thinning and binning that you have, the posterior tree space have way too many configurations (because the chain is still sampling and accepting jumps) and the NULL cutoff tree configuration frequency is 0.05. As a result, all of your posterior configurations have frequencies < 0.05. A very quick fix to get a maximum-likelihood tree is to set post.config.cutoff = 0.01 but I would STRONGLY recommend that you sample longer.

I will update our website/package to give warnings/notes on this. Thanks for bringing this into our attention. Let me know if you have any questions.

Cheers,
Yuchao

--
Yuchao Jiang (yuc...@mail.med.upenn.edu)
PhD student in Genomics and Computational Biology
University of Pennsylvania

